                 "Outcome: About 45 findings, applied to the theory: settings and headings in French that gave Sam a gender, a Korean gloss in 반말 among 해요체, Korean glosses that now add 씨 as the cards do, the supine explained in Korean rather than named, Spanish words set in italics as if Swedish now in «», Spanish and German glosses closer to the Swedish, notes that adapt better to German (Ni as ihr or Sie), and terms made the same in both halves. Two findings asked for card answers to change (Tu vis seul ?, ¿Vives solo?); the cards are left as version 1 has them, so their glosses still match their answers."@en .

